[Music]  what is up everybody its Anna Mack here  for anime uproar and in this video we  will be talking about whether fans of  Dragon Ball Z who might have grown up  with the show or even gone into anime  because of DBZ should bother watching  Dragon Ball super which is the ongoing  sequel to Dragon Ball Z that premiered  almost 20 years after Dragon Ball Z  finished airing I decided to make this  video because I'm one of the people who  grew up watching Dragon Ball Z back in  the early 2000s when the show finally  made its way to North America and as a  huge DBZ fan I was very skeptical about  Dragon Ball super at first in fact I  didn't watch it for a long time after it  started airing because I was afraid that  the show would somehow ruin my childhood  memories but about a year after it first  started airing I finally decided to  catch up on Dragon Ball super and now  I'm going to tell you whether Dragon  Ball super is worth watching in my  opinion we made a poll on our Twitter  about what type of Dragon Ball content  you want to see us make here on the  channel and this topic of Dragon Ball Z  versus Dragon Ball super one the last  poll so that is why I'm making this  video for you guys if you want to take  part in future polls to help us decide  what type of videos to make next you can  follow us on Twitter and we are also  posting daily on Instagram at anime  uproar for both links are in the  description if you end up enjoying this  video and you want to see more don't  forget to subscribe and hit that  notification bell thank you to rift e  beets for the background music he makes  cool remixes of anime soundtracks  including dragon ball music you can  check out his channel link in the  description now the question of whether  a fan of Dragon Ball Z will enjoy Dragon  Ball super is a subjective one if you  watch Dragon Ball Z as a child and liked  it but now that you've gotten older you  only enjoy mature and serious anime  movies TV shows and so on the Dragon  Ball super is probably not for you  Dragon Ball super has it's serious  moments just like Dragon Ball Z did but  overall it is an action anime that  focuses on fighting and advance  sure if you're looking for a deeply  philosophical anime that will make you  think about the meaning of life Dragon  Ball super is not the perfect choice  however Dragon Ball super does offer  four unique things that I think a fan of  John Ball Z will appreciate number one  is world building if you loved the  unique and interesting world of Dragon  Ball Z including the incredible  abilities that the characters possess  and the universe that the story takes  place in then Dragon Ball super does  have a lot to offer in Dragon Ball super  we learned a lot more about the universe  of Dragon Ball and not just one universe  we learned that there are multiple  universes that exist and that the  universe we know from Dragon Ball Z is  just one of those universes in Dragon  Ball super we get to explore and learn  more about not just universe 7 where the  Z fighters come from but also the other  universes and the complex governing  structure that rules over these  universes and this also includes a wide  variety of God's angels and other divine  beings speaking of which in Dragon Ball  super we meet a huge number of new and  interesting characters from the  different universes and beyond  and this really adds to the complexity  and nuance of the world of Dragon Ball  and Dragon Ball super it's not just the  case of the same heroes fighting a new  villain in each art and then moving on  instead we meet a whole bunch of new and  unique characters some good some evil  and some who are in between those two  extremes if you liked the world of  Dragon Ball Z and you're interested in  seeing new planets new characters of  different species and races new divine  beings new and unique abilities and  powers then you should strongly consider  watching Dragon Ball super whether or  not you like the world of Dragon Ball Z  as a fan of the series you definitely  like the characters that we meet along  the way at least some of them anyway if  you've been wondering what happens to  Goku Gohan Vegeta and Bulma Crillon and  Android 18 and everybody else after the  Kid Buu saga Dragon Ball super reveals  this in great detail you get to see how  the relationships between the characters  develop how they start and grow  their families what they do with their  lives how they continue to interact with  each other and so on just to give you  one example I personally really enjoyed  seeing how Vegeta and go Han have  developed into family man who care  deeply for their wives and children and  I love seeing these characters that I've  known since childhood grow evolve and  develop new relationships with each  other there is of course a lot of humor  involved here like in the relationship  between Paul mine Vegeta for example and  I really enjoyed that comedic element as  well when I was first watching Dragon  Ball Z as a kid my favorite character in  the whole show was Future Trunks I loved  how after the epic frieza saga on Namek  where goku struggled for so long to  defeat Frieza Future Trunks just swoops  in and annihilates Frieza and his father  in mere seconds I also loved how Future  Trunks came from a very dark timeline  where he developed into a much different  person than he would have if he had  lived in the present timeline and of  course I appreciated Future Trunks his  sense of fashion including his badass  jacket and sword probably the biggest  reason why I decided to finally give  Dragon Ball super a chance was when I  heard that Future Trunks comes back in  the series and that we get to learn more  about the future timeline and I have to  say I loved learning more about trunks  and seeing the development of his  relationship with characters in the  present timeline especially his  relationship with Vegeta and go Han this  is one of the highlights of Dragon Ball  super for me and if you are one of the  people who loved the main characters in  Dragon Ball Z and you are curious to see  what happens to them next and how their  relationships developed Dragon Ball  super is definitely worth your time in  my opinion number three is pacing and  battle strategy if you're a fan of  Dragon Ball you've got to be a fan of  action and epic battles between  incredibly strong opponents and Dragon  Ball super definitely delivers on this  aspect of the franchise we meet new  insanely powerful characters and this  forces our heroes to get stronger in  order to defeat them and in this sense  there are many similarities to Dragon  Ball Z however there are a few  interesting developments that I see  enjoy  of all super for one the pacing is not  nearly as slow as the original  Dragonball Z in which a single fight  could take nearly 20 episodes and this  was especially hard to deal with when  you were watching the episodes weekly on  TV  in 2009 Dragon Ball Z Kai was released  and it cut out a lot of the slow pacing  and a filler and I think Dragon Ball  super also does a pretty good job of  keeping a fast pace and limiting the  filler to a reasonable extent there is  definitely some filler but I didn't find  it to be as bad as something like the  garlic jr. saga in Dragon Ball Z and  most fights even the epic ones last two  or three episodes not 10 or 20 now some  may disagree with me on this and that's  totally cool but in my opinion Dragon  Ball super at certain times has a bigger  focus on battle strategy then Dragon  Ball Z especially once the big  tournament of power arc gets going  rather than just introducing new more  powerful villains which in turn inspires  everyone to obtain a higher power level  in order to defeat them with pure force  dragon ball super introduces the concept  of a tournament in which multiple teams  of ten fighters must work together to  defeat the other teams and survive this  concept forces us to think about the  importance of teamwork of strategy and  of unique techniques and abilities that  can allow fighters to get the better of  an opponent who is much stronger than  them in terms of physical power alone  once the tournament of power starts it  is also difficult to tell who is the  hero and who is the villain or better  yet maybe there is no villain at all and  that is something that I appreciate life  is often complicated and sometimes there  is no clear-cut good guys and bad guys  just people trying their best to survive  and the tournament of power arc does a  great job of bringing this to life if  that sounds like something that you  might enjoy then Dragon Ball super and  the universe survival saga in particular  is definitely worth watching and number  four is more strong female characters in  Dragon Ball Z we had some notable female  characters including Bulma and chichi of  course and later on in the series  Android 18 Vidal and so on however  Dragon Ball Z  still clearly dominated by male  characters whereas in Dragon Ball super  we meet a lot more badass female  characters including female sands more  strong female fighters from other  universes and powerful female deities  and divine beings I personally enjoyed  seeing all of these new female  characters entered the mix especially  vados who is probably my number one  waifu pick in Dragon Ball with Android  18 a close second let me know who your  favorite female characters are in the  Dragon Ball franchise and in general  tell me how you think Dragon Ball super  stacks up against Dragon Ball Z if  you've already seen Super are you glad  that you gave it a chance and would you  recommend it to your friends give me  your thoughts down in the comments  personally I definitely think that  Dragon Ball super is worth your time if  you enjoyed Dragon Ball or Dragon Ball Z  of course the show isn't perfect but  neither was the original Dragon Ball or  Dragon Ball Z so I definitely think the  show is worth watching and worth your  time but at the end of the day everyone  will make that decision for themselves  and we all have different tastes and  opinions and that's totally cool if you  enjoyed this video and want to see more  dragon ball content in the future be  sure to leave a like to let me know if  you are new to the channel don't forget  to subscribe and hit that notification  bell follow us on Twitter and Instagram  for daily updates at anime uproar and  until next time SIA space cowboys  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]

